  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Players take turns placing cards on the table to 'build' a house.\n2. **Valleys**: Two cards placed side-by-side on the base.\n3. **Floors**: A horizontal card placed over a 'valley'.\n4. **Peaks (Triangles)**: Two cards leaning against each other over a floor.\n5. Points are awarded when a triangle is closed. If the majority of cards in a specific 'story' or triangle are of your color, you score the face value of those cards.",
    Player: "1. Players take turns placing cards on the table to 'build' a house.\n2. **Valleys**: Two cards placed side-by-side on the base.\n3. **Floors**: A horizontal card placed over a 'valley'.\n4. **Peaks (Triangles)**: Two cards leaning against each other over a floor.\n5. Points are awarded when a triangle is closed. If the majority of cards in a specific 'story' or triangle are of your color, you score the face value of those cards.",
    objective: 'Score the most points by forming specific geometric patterns (triangles) using your assigned color.',
    gameplay: "1. Players take turns placing cards on the table to 'build' a house.\n2. **Valleys**: Two cards placed side-by-side on the base.\n3. **Floors**: A horizontal card placed over a 'valley'.\n4. **Peaks (Triangles)**: Two cards leaning against each other over a floor.\n5. Points are awarded when a triangle is closed. If the majority of cards in a specific 'story' or triangle are of your color, you score the face value of those cards.",
    keyRules: [
      'Build from base: valleys (two cards side-by-side), then floors (horizontal over a valley), then peaks (two cards leaning over a floor).',
      'When a triangle is closed, the player whose color holds the majority in that story scores the face value of those cards.',
      'Players take turns placing one card at a time to extend the structure.',
    ],
